      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0001",
      "sequence": 856,
      "meaning": "Hanumān jokes that the small ocean could be crossed repeatedly: the submarine fire of the Lord’s majesty first dried its water, and the tears of the enemy’s women later refilled it and made it salty. The monkeys rejoice. Jāmbavān tells Nala and Nīla to remember Rāma’s power and build the bridge without strain, then commands the bear and monkey hosts to hold Rāma’s lotus feet in their hearts and bring mountains and trees. With cries of victory they lift immense peaks and trees as playthings and deliver them to Nala and Nīla, who construct the causeway.",
