    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0002",
      "sequence": 857,
      "meaning": "As monkeys bring vast mountains, Nala and Nīla catch them like balls. Delighted by the beautiful bridge, Rāma calls the ground supremely lovely and resolves to establish Śambhu there. Sugrīva summons eminent sages; Rāma installs the liṅga with due worship and declares no one dearer to him than Śiva. One who claims devotion to Rāma while opposing Śiva can never attain him, and one who seeks Rāma’s devotion while turning from Śaṅkara is foolish and hell-bound. Whoever loves one Lord but hates the other dwells in dreadful hell for an age.",
