    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0003",
      "sequence": 858,
      "meaning": "Rāma promises that those who behold Rāmeśvara will leave the body for his abode; one who brings Gaṅgā water as an offering will gain union, and Śaṅkara will grant Rāma-bhakti to the desireless, guileless worshipper. Whoever sees Rāma’s bridge will cross becoming without labour. The sages return home. Śiva tells Girijā that Raghupati always loves the surrendered. By Rāma’s grace the bridge built by skilled Nala and Nīla becomes renowned: stones that normally sink or make others sink float like boats. The wonder belongs neither to the sea, stones nor monkeys, but to Raghubīra’s glory; dull are those who abandon him for another lord.",
