    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0004",
      "sequence": 859,
      "meaning": "The monkeys finish an exceedingly firm bridge, pleasing the compassionate Lord, and the indescribable army advances roaring. From the bridge Rāma looks mercifully across the sea; to behold him, every sea creature appears—crocodiles, alligators, fish and serpents of immense size, some able to devour others that themselves terrify the rest. They gaze upon the Lord and cannot be moved; hidden behind their bodies, even the water disappears as they become absorbed in Hari’s form. At Rāma’s order the immeasurable host crosses: the bridge is so crowded that some monkeys fly, while others climb over the creatures and pass across.",
