      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0005",
      "sequence": 860,
      "meaning": "Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa smile at this wonder and descend across the sea with the army, surrounded by innumerable monkey commanders. Camped on the farther shore, Rāma permits all to eat lovely fruits and roots. Trees fruit for his sake regardless of season; bears and monkeys eat sweet fruit, shake trees, and hurl peaks toward Laṅkā. Whenever they find a night-ranger, they surround and torment him, bite off nose and ears, proclaim the Lord’s fame, and release him. The mutilated report everything to Rāvaṇa. Hearing that the ocean—called by every name—has truly been bound, his ten mouths rise in agitation.",
