    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0006",
      "sequence": 861,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa recollects his agitation, forces a laugh and goes home with fear-clouded judgment. Mandodarī hears that the Lord has come and playfully bridged the sea. Taking her husband by the hand to a private chamber, she bows, spreads her veil at his feet and asks him to set anger aside. One should fight only an opponent whom intellect and strength can defeat: between Rāvaṇa and Raghupati lies the distance between a firefly and the sun. Rāma killed mighty Madhu and Kaiṭabha, destroyed Diti’s heroic sons, bound Bali and slew Sahasrabāhu, and has descended to relieve Earth’s burden; Time, action and every life are in his hand. She begs Rāvaṇa to surrender Jānakī, give the kingdom to his son, retire to the forest and worship Raghunātha.",
