      "sequence": 864,
      "meaning": "Prahasta says foolish ministers merely please their master and did not come forward when one monkey crossed the sea: if they were not hungry, why did none seize and eat him while he burned the city? Rāvaṇa suffered by heeding such advice. The one who bridged the ocean effortlessly now camps at Suvela with his army; it is vain to boast that he is only a man fit to eat. Prahasta urges his father not to mistake frank counsel for cowardice. People who offer and accept only pleasing words are plentiful; rare are those who give or hear hard but beneficial speech. Policy says first send an envoy, return Sītā and restore friendship. If Rāma departs with her, do not enlarge the quarrel; otherwise meet him resolutely in battle.",
