      "meaning": "Prahasta says this course will bring Rāvaṇa fame either way. Enraged, Rāvaṇa asks who taught his foolish son such thinking and calls him a rootless reed already hollow with doubt. Prahasta replies harshly and leaves; sound advice no more pleases one ruled by death than medicine at the fatal hour. At twilight Rāvaṇa goes to a marvellous arena atop Laṅkā, seats himself in the palace, and enjoys Kinnara songs, drums, vīṇā and expert celestial dance. Though a foe mightier than a hundred Indras stands over his head, he sports without anxiety or fear.",
